course: dictionary
lesson: 12708
title: Dominated: more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Dominated» comes from the verb dominate. Dominate means to control someone or something, or to be the strongest or the most noticeable. The past form, dominated, tells us it has already happened. «The country was dominated by its neighbour» means the neighbour was more powerful and ruled it.
explain: Sports reports and descriptions of places use it too. «Our team dominated the match» means we were the strongest and had the ball most of the time. «The castle dominated the skyline» means it was the biggest, most noticeable thing you could see from far away.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in another word: controlled, was the strongest, or was the most noticeable. If one of them fits the sentence, you have found the meaning. «Dominated» can also describe a group. «A male-dominated job» means mostly men make up or run that job, which shows an imbalance.
fact: Dominate means to control, or to be the strongest or most noticeable.
fact: «Dominated» is the past form of dominate, so it describes something that has already happened.
fact: «Dominated» can mean ruled or controlled by someone more powerful, as in «The country was dominated by its neighbour».
fact: «Male-dominated» means mostly made of or run by one group, such as men.
fact: In science, a habitat can be dominated by one species that takes over most of the space and food.
exercise: «The country was dominated by its neighbour.» What does dominated mean? | Painted in bright colours | *Ruled or controlled by someone more powerful | Made into a new country | Visited by lots of tourists
exercise: «Our team dominated the match.» What does dominated mean here? | Fell over in the mud | Lost every point | *Was the strongest and had the ball most of the time | Watched from the stands
exercise: «The tall tower dominated the skyline.» What does dominated mean here? | Was hidden behind the trees | *Was the biggest and most noticeable thing | Was closed for repairs | Was made of wood
test: «A male-dominated job» means a job that is mostly done by one group. What does male-dominated mean? | *Mostly made of or run by men | Paid very little money | Only open to people who are fast runners | Full of very loud noise
test: Ben says «dominated» always means happy. Is he right? | Yes, it means the same as helped | Yes, it always means happy | *No, it can mean ruled by someone more powerful | No, it is a sound effect
exam: «In the story, a bully dominated the playground.» What does this show? | *The bully controlled and frightened the others | Everyone was asleep in the sun | The playground was closed for the day | The bully was kind and helped everyone
